// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #5886 Add Socat Reverse Shell Detection Rule for Linux Process Creation
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/5886
// Pull request author: nedelcubianca
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Socat Reverse Shell Execution
// Sigma ID: 004985ba-4624-41ce-8d59-52b0fa8f9518
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: nedelcubianca
// Date: 2026-02-27 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059
// Description: Detects execution of socat with parameters commonly associated with establishing a reverse
//   shell. Socat is a multipurpose relay tool that can be abused to create encrypted or unencrypted
//   reverse shells. This rule covers both plain TCP and SSL/TLS encrypted variants.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of socat for system administration or debugging purposes
// References:
//   - https://pentestmonkey.net/cheat-sheet/shells/reverse-shell-cheat-sheet
//   - https://www.revshells.com/
//   - https://linux.die.net/man/1/socat
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/52069bed37a36f02d289f934c212b5afa13de712/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_socat_reverse_shell.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/socat" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "exec:" or ProcessCommandLine contains "system:") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "bash" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/bin/sh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/bin/bash" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/bin/zsh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/bin/ash" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/bin/csh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/bin/ksh") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "tcp:" or ProcessCommandLine contains "tcp-connect:" or ProcessCommandLine contains "tcp4:" or ProcessCommandLine contains "tcp6:" or ProcessCommandLine contains "ssl:" or ProcessCommandLine contains "ssl-connect:" or ProcessCommandLine contains "openssl:" or ProcessCommandLine contains "openssl-connect:")
